course: dictionary
lesson: 13253
title: Glasshouse: a house made of glass
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A glasshouse is a building made mostly of glass, where plants are grown. The glass lets in the sun, and the warm air stays inside. «The seedlings were kept in the glasshouse to stay warm.» Seedlings are baby plants, so the glass helps them grow.
explain: Look at the clues in a sentence. «The tomatoes grew big and red in the glasshouse, because the sun warmed it all day.» The sun and the warm are the clues. A glasshouse is a place where plants grow in the warm.
explain: Another word for glasshouse is greenhouse. In science, a glasshouse helps explain the «greenhouse effect», because the glass traps the sun's heat, just as a glasshouse keeps plants warm.
fact: A glasshouse is a building made mostly of glass where plants are grown.
fact: A glasshouse is kept warm by the sun, so tender plants can grow well inside it.
fact: Glasshouse means the same as greenhouse.
fact: In old British army slang, a glasshouse was a military prison.
fact: The proverb «People who live in glass houses shouldn't throw stones» means: do not criticise others for faults you have yourself.
exercise: «The seedlings were kept in the glasshouse to stay warm.» What is a glasshouse? | A kind of boat made of glass | A wooden shed for garden tools | *A building made mostly of glass where plants grow | A large window in a school hall
exercise: «The tomatoes grew sweet and red because the sun warmed the glasshouse all day.» What kept the glasshouse warm? | The rain | The wind | The snow | *The sun
exercise: The proverb says, «People who live in glass houses shouldn't throw stones.» What does it mean? | *Do not criticise others for faults you have yourself | Glass breaks easily when it rains | Keep your windows clean | Plants need stones to grow
test: «Mia's glasshouse was full of tomatoes and peppers.» Which word means the same as glasshouse here? | Kitchen | *Greenhouse | Cellar
test: In science, why is it warm inside a glasshouse? | It is built under the ground | *It traps the sun's heat | It is painted black | It has a fire burning inside
exam: «The tender plants grew well in the glasshouse.» Why did they grow well? | The glass made them grow faster by shouting at them | *The glass kept the sun's heat in and the plants warm | They were watered with juice | The glass kept them warm, like a greenhouse
